{# Gotenberg's own running footer for the progression export - a COMPLETE, standalone document,
   which is what Chromium expects of a footer template.

   Two things about it are not negotiable, and both were learned the hard way from the version this
   replaces (a `position: fixed` band inside the document, which Chromium repeated across the top of
   every page):

   - it inherits nothing from index.html - no stylesheet, no font, no variable - so everything it
     needs is written here, inline;
   - Chromium renders it with a default font-size of zero unless one is stated, and clips it to the
     page's bottom margin, so the margin (see App\Service\ProgressionQualiopiExporter) has to be
     tall enough for this band.

   Two layout choices are not cosmetic, both measured against Gotenberg rather than assumed:

   - a TABLE, not flexbox: Chromium ignores `display: flex` here, and the three cells came out
     concatenated ("… test1/2Édité le …");
   - an explicit 186mm width (A4 210mm less the two 12mm side margins) rather than `100%` + padding:
     the percentage resolves against something wider than the printable area, and the right-hand
     cell was cut off mid-word at the paper's edge. Both numbers must move together with the
     exporter's margins.

   `pageNumber` and `totalPages` are Chromium's own classes, filled at print time - the reason the
   document can now number its pages at all. #}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="fr">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<style>
    body { margin: 0; font-family: 'Source Sans 3', 'Segoe UI', Arial, sans-serif;
           font-size: 7.5pt; color: #6b7688; -webkit-print-color-adjust: exact; print-color-adjust: exact; }
    table.f { width: 186mm; margin: 0 auto; border-collapse: collapse; border-top: 0.5pt solid #d3dae4; }
    table.f td { padding-top: 1.2mm; }
    .f__mid { color: #8a93a3; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<table class="f">
    <tr>
        <td align="left">{{ docTitle }}</td>
        <td align="center" class="f__mid">page <span class="pageNumber"></span>/<span class="totalPages"></span></td>
        <td align="right">Édité le {{ generatedAt|date('d/m/Y') }} · MonCampus</td>
    </tr>
</table>
</body>
</html>
